Article 8 (Duties of Stationed Military Attaches)
Stationed military attaches shall perform the following duties:
1. Activities relating to defense diplomacy and defense exchanges and cooperation, and support therefor;
2. Collection and reporting of information affecting national security;
3. Support concerning the import and export of defense industry materiel;
4. Public relations activities directed at the receiving State and military attaches from other States assigned there;
5. Cooperation and support concerning overseas military deployments;
6. Support for military personnel dispatched to the receiving State and protection of civilian military employees and personnel of organizations under the Ministry of National Defense;
7. Management of liaison officers and personnel receiving commissioned training who are dispatched to the receiving State;
8. Assistance to the head of the diplomatic mission abroad concerning military affairs;
9. Other matters instructed by the Minister of National Defense or the head of the diplomatic mission abroad.
